{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793372056,"nonce":"PQC4VAX5fEoYaPs7yiildQZZkoU=","title":"A live RGBA surface for frames another process produces (RayDE framework previews)","message":"**Asked by**\n\nRayDE (rayde-00): app previews for OpenFL, HaxeFlixel, Heaps, Lime and Ceramic run headless in workspace compute; RayDE presents their frames on an Ashui surface and sends input back.\n\n**Today**\n\n- No updatable pixel surface. `ashui.types.Bitmap` decodes and displays only; `ImageAtlas.upload` is internal and takes a rectangle of an atlas.\n- `\u003ccanvas paint\u003e` gets a `CanvasFrame` with the device, encoder and queue, so a canvas can own a texture and call `writeTexture` itself, but nothing packages that, and it does not lay out with fit or scale like `\u003cimage\u003e`.\n- Studio bfb06d5 is planned, not started, and carries scene or frame records, not pixel streams.\n- Input on an element: pointer down, up, move, enter, leave and wheel with a button; key down and up with `repeat`; text input and composition; focus and blur. Missing: pointer capture (there is only `captureWheel`) and touch.\n\n**Wanted**\n\nA `\u003csurface\u003e` element (or a `Canvas` prop) with a texture made once at (w, h), `write(bytes, x, y, w, h)` for dirty rectangles, `object-fit` style fit, clipping and opacity as an `\u003cimage\u003e`, plus pointer capture and touch events on elements.\n\n**Open**\n\nThe cost of one 1280x720 upload per frame in a page (3.7 MB; wasm heap and the copy to the GPU) is unmeasured.","files":null}]}